WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.133
-It is so great to see you.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:04.968
-You see, after "SNL," I dance.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.734
I work in this building now.

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:08.434
-You have an ID here now.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.167
You were great hosting
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.200
Congratulations.
That was fantastic.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.767
Were you nervous going into it?

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.601
-Oh, my gosh.
I was freaking out.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.133
On Monday,
I got there and I was like,

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.133
"There's no way
I can get through this week."

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.601
-Oh, really?
-And then -- Yeah.

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:26.100
I mean, no one can prepare you
for that, whatever they say.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.934
Just so much going, you know,
going on

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.667
and coming at you,
and it's terrifying.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:33.167
But, you know --

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.400
You know, you just have to
make fun of yourself

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.868
and don't take it seriously
and just kind of go with it.

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.834
-And at the end,
don't you feel like...

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:42.501
-And then on Saturday, I was
begging them to bring me back.

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:43.868
-Yeah.

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:45.234
-I was like,
"Please have me again."

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:46.634
-Yeah.
When you're done, you're like,

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:48.000
"Alright.
Let's do it one more time."

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.734
-It's incredible.
It's the best experience ever.

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:52.501
-You mentioned in your monologue
that you're about to

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:53.868
become a U.S. citizen.

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:55.501
-I am.
-So that's exciting.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:56.667
-Well, I think so.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.501
The guy, after the interview,
he was like,

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:00.200
"Yeah, you're approved.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.767
So make sure
you don't do anything

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:03.067
before the oath ceremony."

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:05.200
I'm like,
"What am I going to do?"

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.467
-Yeah. Wow.
-What?!

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:09.167
-You don't know when the
ceremony is? Or it's soon?

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.467
-I do. Next month. Yeah.
-Next month. Congratulations.

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:12.601
-Yeah. It's pretty cool.

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:14.467
-You're gonna be a U.S. citizen.
It's a big deal.

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:16.968
-Yeah, it's a big deal.
I love it. Yeah.

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.267
It's very special.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:19.968
-How long have you been
in the U.S.?

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:22.067
-I think about eight years.

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:24.000
-Yeah. Eight years.
-Seven, eight. I don't know.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.033
-And New York City
was the first place you came to?

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:27.567
-I did, yeah. This was --

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:30.467
The first time I ever came
to the U.S. was New York.

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:35.367
And this is where I found my --
my little dog, Elvis.

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:37.901
Yeah.
-No way.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:40.167
-This is where Elvis --
-Elvis is a New Yorker.

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.701
-Yeah.
-Yeah. It was meant to be.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.567
-Why did you -- Elvis?

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.133
-I was going out and about
in New York,

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:46.934
and I got in the wrong subway,

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.968
so I had to go up
to the street again

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:50.701
to get, you know, downtown.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:54.801
And he was there in the --
in a window, in the glass.

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:57.601
And I was like,
"That's my dog."

00:01:57.601 --> 00:02:04.167
So all my girlfriends went back
to Spain with new bags

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:07.167
and, you know,
clothes and new fashion.

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:09.501
And I went back with a dog.
-Yeah.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:11.667
And why did you name him Elvis?

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.000
-Elvis is -- At the time,

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.534
I was just listening a lot
to Elvis Presley.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:16.901
It was what was going on.

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:19.167
It was my ring phone --
like the ringtone.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.968
And it was all about Elvis.
-I love that.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:26.701
Well, it's been such a year
for you because not only "SNL"

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:29.234
and not only,
of course, citizenship,

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:31.133
but you also were nominated
for an Oscar.

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:33.300
Congratulations for that.
Well-deserved.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.067
-Thank you.
-Well-deserved.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:38.801
You were so great in "Blonde."

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:40.434
How did it feel?
What were the Oscars --

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:42.801
What did it feel like?
Was it amazing? Was it --

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.667
-It was -- It was amazing.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:47.367
-It was --
It was also an experience

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.834
that you can only, you know --

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:52.133
You have to be there
to know what it feels like.

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:53.434
It was pretty surreal.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:54.534
-Yeah.
-It was awesome.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:56.100
-Did you end up
meeting new friends?

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.934
Did you sit at a fun table?
-A lot of people.

00:02:57.934 --> 00:02:59.767
You meet a lot of people --
all these actors

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:01.567
that you've always been,
you know,

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:04.501
looking up to
and admiring their work.

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:07.467
There was one in particular that
I was very, very happy to meet.

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:09.901
-Yeah, and this is Ke.
Ke Huy Quan.

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:12.200
-Yeah.
-Yeah. Who won an Oscar.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.534
-Who won an Oscar.
Who won everything. Yeah.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:17.767
-How did you meet him at first?
-I met him --

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:21.100
I was at the Governors Ball.
-Yeah.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.567
-And he came to me.
And I was by myself.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.534
And I didn't know who he was,
and he asked me for a selfie.

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:30.601
And then, of course, you know,
if you've seen his Instagram,

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:33.434
he posts selfies
with everybody.

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:35.934
And my boyfriend saw the selfie
and he was like,

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:37.701
"Oh, my God! You met Ke!"

00:03:37.701 --> 00:03:40.100
And I'm like, "Yeah.
Who are you talking about?"

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.734
He's like,
"He's Data from 'The Goonies'!"

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:44.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:45.567
-He is!
-And I'm like, "What?!"

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:47.901
-Yeah, I know,
but I grew up, like --

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:49.934
For some reason in Cuba,
they would play "The Goonies"

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:51.400
all the time on TV.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.834
Like, this was one of my
favorite movies ever growing up,

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:57.868
and I didn't realize that Ke
was the guy from "The Goonies."

00:03:57.868 --> 00:04:00.467
-Yeah, he was a kid at the time.
Yeah. Now he's a man.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:02.200
-This selfie was so horrible.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.801
I'm so serious because
I'm like, "Hm." I don't know.

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:07.400
-You didn't know him.
-I just didn't know.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.400
I didn't get excited.
-But then you saw him again.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.801
-I saw him, and I was like --

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:14.033
I ran to him and I was like,
"I need a selfie with you!"

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:17.100
-Yeah. Exactly. Right.
-Then I was very, very happy.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.100
Of course.
-Well, I have two pictures.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.734
I have two selfies.

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:23.400
Here's the one that he took when
you didn't really recognize him.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:28.701
And then here's the one
after you went up to him.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:32.534
You're like, "Oh, yeah! Hey!"

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:34.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:37.367
-Yeah.

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:39.667
-Let's talk about --
Let's talk about your new movie.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:41.801
"Ghosted."
It's with Chris Evans.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:44.234
Gosh. He's just fantastic.
He was here last night.

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:46.234
-I saw it.
-You guys are great together.

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:47.934
This is your third movie
you've done together?

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:50.834
-Yeah. Third movie together.
-"Knives Out."

00:04:50.834 --> 00:04:52.667
-Yeah, we met in "Knives Out"
and "Gray Man."

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:54.067
-"Gray Man."
-And now "Ghosted."

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:57.601
-Yeah. So you've thrown up
on him in "Knives Out."

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.133
You've killed --
You've shot him.

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:02.267
-Yes. I shot him in the butt.
-Yes. And now you --

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:04.167
-Threw up on his face.

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:06.534
And in this one,
I'm trying to --

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:08.667
Well, I kiss him.
I'm nice to him.

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:10.801
-You save him.
-I save him.

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:13.033
-You save his life.
-Even better. Yeah.

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:15.434
-Yeah.
-The idea -- I love it.

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:17.567
It's basically you guys,

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:21.300
two beautiful-looking people,
meet, and they go,

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.000
"Oh, let's go on maybe a date."

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.033
So they go on a date,
and then you ghost him.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:27.567
-Well, I'm working.
-Yeah, but he doesn't know that.

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:29.601
He doesn't know.
And so he goes, "Wait."

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:31.534
So he got ghosted by you.
He's like --

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:34.801
But then he realizes that
he forgot that you have his --

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.934
-I got his inhaler,
which has one of those.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:40.133
-He put an Apple Tag on it.
So he can track you.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:42.167
And he's like, "Wait.
I'm going to find out.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:44.167
Maybe it will be romantic.
She's in London.

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:45.901
I'll go surprise her
and be like..."

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:47.634
-Don't do that, people.
Don't show up.

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:49.801
-Yeah. It's called stalking.
Don't do that. Yeah.

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.501
-Don't do that.
-Don't do that. Yeah.

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:54.067
But he's embarrassed. He's like,
"Alright. I took it too far.

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:56.367
I texted her too much.
That's why she's ghosting me."

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:58.234
Then he finds out
you're a secret agent.

00:05:58.234 --> 00:05:59.834
-Yeah.
-You're a spy.

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:03.033
And you are a kick-ass spy.
You're fantastic at it.

00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:04.934
-I try. Yeah.

00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:06.701
-Yeah. I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:06:06.701 --> 00:06:08.601
Here's Ana de Armas
and Chris Evans

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:11.234
in "Ghosted" on Apple TV+.
Take a look.

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:13.767
-I really ate it up, too,
didn't I?

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:16.467
Especially that sob story
about your coworker that died.

00:06:16.467 --> 00:06:18.534
That is low!

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:21.767
-That was actually true.
Her name was Elena.

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:23.367
-And she really died?

00:06:26.601 --> 00:06:29.033
-I may have killed her.

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:31.234
-What?!

00:06:31.234 --> 00:06:35.033
-She was an enemy agent.
She worked for these guys.

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:36.968
-You said she was a coworker.

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:38.567
-She was -- in a loose sense.

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:40.200
-See, this is what
I'm talking about.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.834
It's just lies and lies
and more lies.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:43.501
-It's no lies and more lies.

00:06:43.501 --> 00:06:45.767
It's the sub-lie
of the first original lie.

00:06:45.767 --> 00:06:47.334
-You're unbelievable.

00:06:47.334 --> 00:06:48.734
-Yeah, that's right.

00:06:48.734 --> 00:06:51.300
"Ghosted." Ana de Armas.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:56.834
Last time you were here,

00:06:56.834 --> 00:06:59.400
you were talking about how one
of your favorite ice creams

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.367
is my ice cream,
which is The Tonight Dough.

00:07:02.367 --> 00:07:06.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:06.167 --> 00:07:08.267
And so I loved that so much.

00:07:08.267 --> 00:07:10.734
And that's why I wanted
to celebrate your big year

00:07:10.734 --> 00:07:12.467
by maybe having
a spoonful together.

00:07:12.467 --> 00:07:16.067
-Listen. If you give me ice
cream every time I come here...

00:07:16.067 --> 00:07:17.501
-But wait.
I'm gonna do one better.

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:19.734
Because you said, actually,
if you wanted to change

00:07:19.734 --> 00:07:21.767
the flavor, we were like,
"What would you do?"

00:07:21.767 --> 00:07:23.367
You go,
"Maybe I'd add a little..."

00:07:23.367 --> 00:07:25.133
-Condensed milk.
-Condensed milk.

00:07:25.133 --> 00:07:26.968
Well, our friends at
Ben &amp; Jerry's heard this

00:07:26.968 --> 00:07:29.868
and wanted to send you
a message. Take a look.

00:07:29.868 --> 00:07:32.200
-Hi, Ana. I'm Ben.
-I'm Jerry.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:34.767
-We were so excited to hear

00:07:34.767 --> 00:07:37.300
that Ben &amp; Jerry's
The Tonight Dough

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.734
is your favorite ice cream.

00:07:38.734 --> 00:07:41.501
We love that you're a fan
and came up

00:07:41.501 --> 00:07:45.534
with something in our kitchen
for a special one-day-only

00:07:45.534 --> 00:07:47.901
one-time-only surprise.

00:07:47.901 --> 00:07:51.767
-Jimmy, can you show Ana
what we come up with?

00:07:51.767 --> 00:07:53.334
-Since it was
a dream of yours...

00:07:53.334 --> 00:07:55.367
-You're kidding.
-...to have your own flavor,

00:07:55.367 --> 00:07:57.501
we like to make dreams
come true.

00:07:57.501 --> 00:08:00.534
Here's your special
one-time-only

00:08:00.534 --> 00:08:03.100
Ana de ArMAS Leche.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:06.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:06.133 --> 00:08:10.000
-Oh, my God!
-Come on! I'm not kidding!

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.400
You got to try it.
It's condensed milk.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.968
It's condensed milk
in the ice cream.

00:08:15.968 --> 00:08:17.767
Here's the recipe
on how to make it.

00:08:17.767 --> 00:08:20.234
That's your condensed milk
right in the middle there.

00:08:20.234 --> 00:08:21.868
Oh, my God.

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:23.300
-You can see it.
Yeah. There you go.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:24.601
-This is too much.

00:08:24.601 --> 00:08:26.634
-We wanted our studio audience
to join in

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:29.100
on the celebration, too,
so everyone in the audience

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:31.167
is going home with
some Ben &amp; Jerry's tonight

00:08:31.167 --> 00:08:34.267
and the directions
to make the...

00:08:34.267 --> 00:08:37.000
Come on! Ben &amp; Jerry!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.234
Ana de Armas!
Come on, everybody!

00:08:40.234 --> 00:08:43.667
Her movie, "Ghosted,"
premieres globally this Friday

00:08:43.667 --> 00:08:44.701
on Apple TV+.

00:08:44.701 --> 00:08:46.734
Ana and I are playing
a brand-new game

00:08:46.734 --> 00:08:48.467
when we come back.
Stick around.

